<section aria-labelledby="workflow-title" class="workflow wrap" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="workflow-intro">
        <h2 id="workflow-title">Install it once.<br /><em>Remember it forever.</em></h2>
        <p>
            pkg installs through mise and records what you chose in your global config. When it’s
            time for a new machine, your software has a packing list.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="workflow-track">
        <div class="workflow-step">
            <span class="step-marker">1</span>
            <h3>Make yourself at home.</h3>
            <p>Use the package names you already know. pkg handles the install through mise.</p>
            <div class="workflow-code">
                <span class="code-label">YOUR TERMINAL</span
                ><code><span class="muted">$</span> pkg install brew:wget</code>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step">
            <span class="step-marker">2</span>
            <h3>Keep the packing list.</h3>
            <p>Your global mise config remembers. Keep it in your dotfiles and bring it along.</p>
            <div class="workflow-code">
                <span class="code-label">GLOBAL MISE CONFIG · EXAMPLE</span>
                <pre><code>[bootstrap.packages]
"brew:wget" = <span class="code-yellow">"latest"</span></code></pre>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step">
            <span class="step-marker">3</span>
            <h3>Unpack somewhere new.</h3>
            <p>Bring your config to a new machine. mise restores the software it declares.</p>
            <div class="workflow-code">
                <span class="code-label">YOUR NEXT MACHINE</span
                ><code><span class="muted">$</span> mise bootstrap</code>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="workflow-footnote">
        Your config stays yours.
        <a href="/docs/configuration">See where pkg writes <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </p>
</section>
